A||||12||batboy||honorable opponent with class||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||05-24-2000||08:18 PM||||I was heading back to work after lunch today. My office is located at the airport, so four lane road I'm driving on is in a semi-rural area. I'm sitting at the last stoplight on the way back, then it's two miles of  open road before my turn-off. A nice early 70's El Camino pulls up next to me. Sounds like a stock 350 to me. The guy looks to be my age or so. He revs and I goose the Batmobile. He smiles, I grin. The light turns green. I ease into the gas just enough to make the dual exhaust bark a little. I hear the El Camino step into it just enough to pull up next to me. I drop the right foot down another notch and the Batmobile leaps to a half car lead. I hear the Chevy crank up some more rpm to draw up next to me again. We are just toying with each other. This guy is probably an old gear head from my era. Half the fun of street racing was the "foreplay" prior to the mad dash. Sometimes, a smart person might back down at this point, if the opponent's engine sounded a bit too good.<P>Regardless, I was ready to drop the hammer the whole way and pop those four barrels open, but glanced up to scope out the situation in front of us, first. His lane was clear, but a 1/4 mile ahead of me in my lane was an econobox car with it's turn signal on. I quickly let up on the gas and poised my foot above the brake pedal. The El Camino saw what was happening and backed off too. The car ahead of us turned off the road and we had open road again. I glanced over and saw we were exactly door to door. I knew he planned it that way. He wanted a fair run. He glanced my way for a split second nodded. We both nailed it at the same time, except the Batmobile was in it's power curve and jumped way out front and started pulling several car lengths. Dang, still have some torque steer problems and wow it's loud and holy guano it's fast.<P>Well, I'm fast approaching my turn off for work and going a wee bit too fast, so I flash my bat taillights three times to signal it's over. As I continue to slow down for my turn, the honorable El Camino pilot pulls up next to me and gives a friendly wave. He is intently scanning my car from tip to stern and probably wondering, "What in the hell just happened?" He looks up again and I salute him. He smiled and saluted me back. What class! I got to remember to lose that graciously...oh please Batmobile, don't let me down...I don't want to lose with dignity and grace...dammit...I want to always win!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Uaana||05-24-2000||08:42 PM||||Damn... It just don't get any better than that.. <BR>Maybe if you had a couple of old issues of Cartoons to curl up with to end your day..<BR>I just have this image of you cruising down the road with just your eyes peering out above the door sill with your hand on the stick as it sticks out of the sun roof.||||reg||14
