Z||000004||Dan86gt3.8||05-25-2000||03:28 AM||||guano=bat crap= you no poo from a bat he's batboy very clever, and yeah a fiero is just a FWD drivetrian turned around backwards (I thinks its from a chevette).  anywyas its rear whell drive but with front wheel drive stuff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||05-25-2000||07:28 AM||||Actually it's the front drivetrain from a Citation. When a high torque engine like a 350 V8 sits sidewise, heavy throttle will cause the engine to twist, but since it's attached to the cradle, it moves the whole cradle along with the rear suspension for a brief second. What this means when you're driving is that when you slam down the gas, you have your hands full for a second when the back of the car suddenly squirms sidewise a bit. I'm eventually going to try poly cradle bushings and a second dogbone to see if that helps.||||reg||1
