Z||000011||olympic||05-27-2000||11:39 PM||||  I'll agree with racer 1.  If your going to replace the bushings you might as well go all the way and get the aluminum ones.  I cant see  them affecting the ride quality at all.  The factory rubber ones were probably meant to absorb engine vibrations not bumps in the road, thats the job of the suspension.||||reg||1
Z||000012||batboy||05-27-2000||11:51 PM||||Maybe you guys are right about the aluminum cradle bushings, who knows. I've heard that the 88 bushings are metal, but we're forgetting one thing here. The front main motor mount on these V8 conversions are a solid steel motor mount. I think I might try the poly cradle bushings along with a second dogbone first. I'm not ready to mount both the cradle and the engine completely solid. That's asking for a lot of vibration and ultimately something breaking, in my opinion.||||reg||1
